-- title:
--   Unit ideles are reduced norms from an Eichler order
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q$ be a prime, and assume [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L87): $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ the completed algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q$ lies in the prime ideal of $v$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an Eichler order of level $N$, that is, $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ (orders maximal for inclusion among orders) with the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ equal to $N$. Let $\varepsilon=(\varepsilon_w)_w$ assign to each finite place $w$ an element $\varepsilon_w$ of the completion $\mathbb{Q}_w$ with $v(\varepsilon_w)=1$. Then there is a unit $u$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ stabilising, under multiplication, the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele all of whose components are integral, such that for every finite place $w$ and every ring isomorphism $\varphi:\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w\simeq\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}_w,a,b]$ acting coordinatewise, i.e. $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot(z_{\mathrm{re}},z_{\mathrm{imI}},z_{\mathrm{imJ}},z_{\mathrm{imK}})$ with the coordinates mapped by $\mathbb{Q}\to\mathbb{Q}_w$, the reduced norm $x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a\,x_{\mathrm{imI}}^2-b\,x_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2+ab\,x_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$ of the $w$-component $\varphi(u_w)$ of $u$ equals $\varepsilon_w$.
--
--   This is the local norm-surjectivity of Eichler orders in a definite rational quaternion algebra: every family of local units at the finite places is the family of reduced norms of the local components of a single element of the idelic unit group $\widehat{R}^{\times}$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_mem_awayUnits_nrd_eq_of_le_isMaximalOrder`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_mem_awayUnits_nrd_eq_of_le_isMaximalOrder).
